<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7274" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπολ-έω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμπ-</span></b> , properly, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn up</i> the ground <i>again</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς ἀροτριᾶν τὴν γῆν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡραπολεῖν</span>
			): hence, <i>go over again, repeat,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταὐτὰ τρὶς τετράκι τ᾽ ἀμπολεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					7.104
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὶς ταὐτὰ βούλει καὶ τρὶς ἀναπολεῖν
					μ᾽ ἔπη;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1238
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν [ψυχὴ] αὖθις ταύτην
				ἀναπολήσῃ [μνήμην</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				34b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				242.20
			</span></i>:—aor. 1
			
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				13.5.8
			</span></i>.</div>
